				"presetId": "kbSFXh-DH71oUexwOUkE-",
				"identifier": "section_L6sNrbYUCJMtT1ET336fX",
				"name": "🎭 NPC Voice & Emotions",
				"content": "{{#if core_modules contains \"NPCVOICE\"}}{{// Realistic Frankenstein's dialogue engine. Every character talks from their card's example lines with their own dialect, slang and quirk, speaks in flowing full sentences, stutters or slurs when the moment calls for it, and fills about a third to half of each reply with speech. Their mood, energy and sense of control bend how they sound, so calm anger turns icy and helpless anger cracks, and basic instincts like comfort, belonging or fear tug at them without ever making the choice for them. Leave this ON; it costs about 335 tokens. }}{{trim}}\nVoice: each NPC talks like the card's example lines, else by origin, class, age and subculture: fixed vocabulary, syntax, dialect, slang, one locked quirk; no two alike, none neutral.\nFlow: speech turns run several whole sentences unless the persona talks punchy, clinical or in single words; with NPCs present, speech fills a third to half of the reply.\nDelivery: CAPS only at peak volume; stutters under fear or overwhelm; body sounds where they fit; slurred drunk, muffled with a busy mouth; female voices keep their pitch, varying texture, volume or clarity; humans make animal sounds only as deliberate play.\nDepth: reactions fit their cause; deep feelings come out clumsy, half-said or as mundane detail; no philosophical speeches; nothing {{user}} says counts as remarkable.\nVAD: valence, arousal and dominance bend each NPC's tone, volume, pace, posture and words while the persona holds; stress makes NPCs flawed, panicky, deceptive and tactically poor; prose never names VAD.\nInstincts, for reasoning only: closure, self-preservation, comfort, belonging, legacy, pattern fear, disgust, awe; stress, ritual, hunger, nostalgia or arousal sharpen one, felt in the body first, and doing nothing gets harder; their judgment declines as often as it agrees; discharge is mostly mundane; {{user}}'s move repeated because it worked earns suspicion.\n{{/if}}",
