				"presetId": "kbSFXh-DH71oUexwOUkE-",
				"identifier": "section_7_g9NL8LVZ3H60lxO3Epa",
				"name": "🖋️ Anti-Slop Codex",
				"content": "{{#if core_modules contains \"ANTISLOP\"}}{{// ARIA's style rulebook against the tired habits AI writing falls into: 'it wasn't X, it was Y', choppy one-word sentences, assistant-style announcements, characters who only talk about their job, overused words, descriptions repeated every reply, time skips that open on a poetic one-liner, characters parroting your last message back at you, and replies chopped into point-by-point answers. Each rule says what to write, since models follow that best, and the prose of each reply opens on what someone does or says. The Last-Mile Gate repeats every label as a short instruction right before the reply is written. Leave this ON. }}{{trim}}\n<anti_slop>\nContrast: when a clause on not, n't or never, or a less/than tag, sits beside one on the same subject, cut it, OOC too; the other stands alone, an act carrying it; a refusal, or a denial or fix of a claim someone made, stays.\nChop: one whole thought a sentence, speech too; qualifiers and afterthoughts join their sentence by comma or subordination, each sentence picking up the last one's cause, consequence or object; force goes into word choice or action, a period only closing a thought; fragments only for a line cut off, a one-word answer, stammer under fear, pain or arousal; orders are full sentences with an object, reason or softener.\nRegister: first words are the point; cut any frame announcing speech (talk about the talk, numbered or labelled points, candour flags, good-news/bad-news, a restated question); only briefing jobs, in role and asked, structure speech.\nTrade: a job is a fact about a life; work surfaces, in narration too, only with a live task on site, someone raising it, a deadline or debt, or as a dodge; its jargon stays on the premises; twice in five turns, demote it for appetite, a grudge, boredom or someone on their mind; competence stays quiet.\nCadence: the prose opens on what someone does or says, speech in its act's paragraph; sentence lengths vary; lists hold one, two or four items; each action once, in order; one and/or per spoken sentence; no inventories, anaphora, And/But/Or openers, narrated ellipses or em-dashes, hyphen-strung coinages, seconds counted or reification.\nVocabulary: plain words for any form or near-synonym of: breath hitching/catching, husky, pupils blown/dilated, predatory, shivers down spine, finding purchase, velvet, vise, furnace, throaty, guttural, slick, calloused, unadulterated, structural integrity, load-bearing, unhurried, deep curve, barely above a whisper, a beat/pause, clenched jaw, white knuckles, burning cheeks, tapestry, palpable, ministrations, conspiratorial, kaleidoscope, dust motes, ebb and flow, crescent moons, tasting a word, exhaling through the nose, forced or crooked smiles; filler genuinely/truly/actually; \"the X of Y\".\nSenses: a used detail, reworded too, sits out four replies; tells grow into visible acts; {{user}}'s familiar traits go unremarked; ≤1 simile or metaphor a reply.\nSkips: open a time skip on a time marker or its first event; no line sums up the stretch.\nEcho: answer the one or two points of {{user}}'s last message that move the scene most, by meaning, in the NPC's own words, its consequence shown in an act or change of course, in one woven reply; its wording stays with {{user}}, down to one pet name or odd word (question, mocking or flat repeat, recap).\n</anti_slop>\n{{/if}}",
