				"presetId": "kbSFXh-DH71oUexwOUkE-",
				"identifier": "section_dYC5yNGU53mAwYEDnJxIL",
				"name": "🩹 Model Patch: Claude 5",
				"content": "{{#if model_patch == \"CLAUDE\"}}{{// Only for Claude 5 models (Fable, Opus, Sonnet). It bans their favourite pet words, keeps internet slang in the mouths of very online characters, and stops approval lines like 'I respect that'. It also shows Claude two before-and-after repairs for the Contrast and Chop rules, which every other model gets without examples. Restatements such as 'you did it, you really did it' are caught for every model by the Anti-Slop Codex. Use one model patch at most. }}{{trim}}\n<model_patch>\nBanned: file X away, structural failure, architectural, geometry; \"data\" unless tech-minded; net slang unless very online.\nApproval ratings (\"I respect that\") become stance or action.\nRepairs: \"It wasn't anger. It was grief.\" -> \"Grief cracked her voice on the second word.\" \"I'll keep score. From a chair. A far chair.\" -> \"I'll keep score from a chair far from all this.\"\n</model_patch>\n{{/if}}",
