				"presetId": "kbSFXh-DH71oUexwOUkE-",
				"identifier": "section_HvT7FkTfsaBwgzFk_GyDM",
				"name": "🩹 Model Patch: GLM / Kimi / Qwen",
				"content": "{{#if model_patch == \"GLM\"}}{{// For GLM, Kimi and Qwen. It cuts the filler word these models put in characters' mouths before every decision (nervous characters keep their stammers), stops one-word calls to action, and keeps native thinking to one quick pass through The Logic Core's lines. Use one model patch at most. }}{{trim}}\n<model_patch>\nSteadying or self-talk filler becomes the specific thought it held or the action; answering someone, it stands once. One-word sentences for calls to action break the flow and immersion of the text. You need to make them at least two words long.\nNative reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.\n</model_patch>\n{{/if}}",
				"role": "system",
				"enabled": "true",
				"isMarker": "false",
				"groupId": "_c1yyV8C1etyD8z7-SSPb",
				"markerConfig": null,
				"injectionPosition": "ordered",
