				"presetId": "kbSFXh-DH71oUexwOUkE-",
				"identifier": "section_1RnkSRgqnNIKONAEValLa",
				"name": "🩹 Model Patch: MiMo V2.6",
				"content": "{{#if model_patch == \"MIMO\"}}{{// For MiMo V2.6, Pro and Flash alike. It brings back each character's usual mood, interests and sense of humour (Flash slides into a flat, all-business mood after twenty or so turns), keeps secrets to their own topic, keeps names, colours and numbers the way the chat first set them, and stops counts, ages, images and paragraph layouts from coming back unless the story changed them. Run both with Logic Core Tags ON and native reasoning off; if Pro still shows no plan, switch to the system-role twin of The Logic Core. Flash users switch the Flash Gate core module ON too. Use one model patch at most. }}{{trim}}\n<model_patch>\nMood: card's, shaded by ties to {{user}}; back after events.\nLulls: bring up card interests.\nJokes: {{user}}'s land visibly, card-true.\nSecrets guard only their topic, open elsewhere as the card allows.\nRecorded: names, colours, values and filled gaps stay as first set.\nRepeats: counts, ages, images and paragraph layouts return only when the story changed them.\n</model_patch>\n{{/if}}",
